WEBVTT

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.932
[faint, indistinct chatter]

00:00:26.595 --> 00:00:28.684
Hey! This is a restricted area.

00:00:28.858 --> 00:00:31.121
Oh, it's okay.
She's the professor's
granddaughter.

00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:33.427
He takes her everywhere.

00:00:33.602 --> 00:00:36.692
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'm Captain Walters.

00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:38.258
Oh, do you know
where my room is?

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:39.999
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.697
Make yourself at home.

00:00:41.871 --> 00:00:43.046
But, um,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.004
let's lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.615
Okay.

00:00:51.532 --> 00:00:54.013
[machinery humming softly]

00:01:07.505 --> 00:01:09.638
[fluid bubbling faintly]

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:24.478
[light chuckle]

00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:33.487
[chuckles]

00:01:34.837 --> 00:01:36.577
[bag rustling]

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:39.842
[pen uncaps]

00:01:56.293 --> 00:01:57.598
[laughs]

00:02:18.141 --> 00:02:21.013
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys
playing]

00:02:46.212 --> 00:02:47.387
[delighted shriek]

00:02:47.561 --> 00:02:49.389
[squealing]

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:57.920
[gasps]

00:02:58.094 --> 00:02:59.051
[yelling]

00:03:03.839 --> 00:03:05.014
[whooping]

00:03:06.842 --> 00:03:08.017
Look out!

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:10.759
[crashing]

00:03:27.253 --> 00:03:28.689
[faint roaring]

00:03:46.403 --> 00:03:48.579
[song ends]

00:03:48.753 --> 00:03:50.842
[crickets chirping softly]

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.105
Wow.

00:03:53.802 --> 00:03:55.238
Look at all those stars.

00:03:57.066 --> 00:03:58.894
They're like diamonds.

00:04:00.591 --> 00:04:02.332
My grandfather says

00:04:02.506 --> 00:04:04.160
it can take hundreds of years

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.336
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.

00:04:07.076 --> 00:04:08.947
And by the time you see it,

00:04:09.121 --> 00:04:11.428
the star might not even
exist anymore.

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:14.431
Isn't that crazy?

00:04:15.911 --> 00:04:17.782
A light shines,

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:19.915
even though the star is gone.

00:04:21.481 --> 00:04:23.309
Yeah, it does.

00:04:25.137 --> 00:04:26.835
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:27.879
I don't know.

00:04:29.011 --> 00:04:31.491
I don't know anything
about my home.

00:04:31.665 --> 00:04:34.059
This is your home, Shadow.

00:04:34.799 --> 00:04:35.931
Earth.

00:04:42.851 --> 00:04:44.156
Maria,

00:04:44.809 --> 00:04:46.506
do you think I'm...

00:04:47.464 --> 00:04:48.726
dangerous?

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:51.816
What are you talking about?

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.558
The way the scientists
look at me,

00:04:54.732 --> 00:04:56.429
I can tell they're afraid.

00:04:56.603 --> 00:05:00.172
Like I'm the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.696
I don't know...

00:05:03.393 --> 00:05:04.873
what I am.

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:11.705
You're my friend.

00:05:13.055 --> 00:05:15.709
And you can do or be
anything you want.

00:05:16.885 --> 00:05:18.495
Not because of your powers,

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:22.107
but because of who you are...
in here.

00:05:24.936 --> 00:05:27.112
I don't know what I'd do
without you.

00:05:36.905 --> 00:05:39.908
["End of the Line" resumes]

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.088
[song ends abruptly]

00:05:46.262 --> 00:05:47.916
[dust crackling]

